Howdy,

Finally beat Slash'em on my iPhone.  Thanks (and curses, from my work
and wife) to Dirk for the port.  Maybe I can stop playing for a while
now...at least until the Enforcer patch gets a coupld fixes.

This was a relatively easy game.  An altar on level 1 made for a very
early Magicbane and Finger of Death.  It took forever to get Magic
Missile, which was annoying, but after that it was pretty
straightforward.  My solution to Vecna, Demogorgon, Angels, & Death
was my (eventually) blessed rustproof +6 submachine gun named Foobane,
with +6 bullets when necessary.  Otherwise Confuse Monster + Magicbane
wreaks havoc in melee and against the non-magic-resistant, I had
spells aplenty.  Plus there was always the backup drow sleep touch,
though I didn't use it much this game.

I only made a couple wishes, despite ending up with 3 magic lamps
along with the usual wand.  I needed a ring of free action, and ended
up getting a magic marker to write enchant armor scrolls.  I left
about a quarter million in gold in my Sokoban cache.

The Plane of Fire was annoying, as I got ganged up on by a bunch of
fire elementals, covering up the portal and delaying me until a Solar
arrived.  That was a near thing, but I teleported him away and drank
full healing and didn't see him again.  I think that was also where
Yeenoghu ended up being marooned, as he couldn't get through the
elemental cloud to stand next to me.  (I had to kill Juiblex after a
bounced spell angered him during my ascent.  I paid off all the demons
that would allow me to - with coin from their own floors - so I only
had to kill Demogorgon and Orcus.)

Otherwise, I made the mistake of trying to teleport Death away, which
cost me 20 points off my max hit points, and I made for the right
altar, decided I was on the wrong path, went to the wrong altar, and
came back, making for a lot of carnage on the Astral Plane.

Yay,
Alex

PS - Are robes of power actually useful to Wizards?  They don't seem
to do anything to 'boost spellpower' as far as I can tell.  I went
with a robe of protection instead.


